                <pb facs="0645" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2221: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-29T16:00:00+09:00">August 29, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 29—8:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1342. The following official statement was released to the press by the
                    Information Board at 2:30 p.m. today: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Ambassador Nomura called on the American President on August 28 and in
                            view of the international conditions of the time he delivered, in the
                            form of a message from Premier Konoye, Japan’s view regarding Pacific
                            problems which are pending between Japan and the United States.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
